; Recovery: which transcript is which permaflow's, read from the
; transcripts themselves, after the Flow Nexus has lost it.
;
; The one input is a Recovery: the transcript root, where a session's start
; stands in a session file, and the marks of its identity lines. Nothing is
; read from the environment and nothing of these is written in the code.
;
; A session file is a file directly in a directory directly under the root
; whose name ends in the FileSuffix. Its identity is read from its records
; whose RecordField holds a KindField equal to SnapshotKind: each string
; under that record's PromptField is read line by line, the line opening
; with the AddressMark giving the Address, the line opening with the
; FlowIdMark the flow id the launcher wrote. The last such record with both
; holds for the file.
;
; Each output line is one Placement. Bind is the meta Signal's Bind input
; (meta-signal-flow 0.95.0), printed as flow-meta reads it, one for each
; Address found: the file written newest of those that claim it. Contested
; names an Address and the other files that claim it; Unidentified a
; session file no identity could be read from.

Library
[ flow_ethos:Address
  signal_flow:TranscriptPath ]
[ TranscriptRoot.String
  FileSuffix.String
  RecordField.String
  KindField.String
  SnapshotKind.String
  PromptField.String
  AddressMark.String
  FlowIdMark.String
  SessionShape.{ FileSuffix RecordField KindField SnapshotKind PromptField }
  IdentityMarks.{ AddressMark FlowIdMark }
  Recovery.{ TranscriptRoot SessionShape IdentityMarks }
  ; The printed form of every output line; Bind is declared here alone.
  Placement.[ Bind.{ Address TranscriptPath }
              Unidentified.TranscriptPath
              Contested.{ Address Vector<TranscriptPath> } ] ]
[]
[]
